---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const breadcrumbSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    {
      '@type': 'ListItem',
      position: 1,
      name: 'Home',
      item: 'https://freeqrcode-generator.com',
    },
    {
      '@type': 'ListItem',
      position: 2,
      name: 'Security',
      item: 'https://freeqrcode-generator.com/security',
    },
  ],
};

const webpageSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Security Architecture & Practices — Free QR Code Generator',
  url: 'https://freeqrcode-generator.com/security',
  description: 'Verified security controls, encryption, client-side isolation, data protection practices, and vulnerability disclosure policies for FreeQRCode-Generator.com.',
  publisher: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'FK Digital Media',
    url: 'https://freeqrcode-generator.com',
  },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Security Architecture & Practices — Free QR Code Generator"
  description="Explore the technical security controls, client-side static isolation, authentication mechanisms, and responsible vulnerability disclosure process at FreeQRCode-Generator.com."
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema, webpageSchema]}
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-6 sm:p-12 shadow-sm space-y-10">

      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="border-b border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800 pb-6 space-y-2">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded-lg text-xs font-semibold bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/60 text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 border border-emerald-200 dark:border-emerald-800">
            Verified Controls
          </span>
          <span class="text-xs text-slate-400">• Last Reviewed: September 2026</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          Security Architecture &amp; Practices
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed pt-1">
          This document describes the high-level security controls, architectural patterns, and defensive measures genuinely implemented across FreeQRCode-Generator.com. We do not use hyperbole or claim absolute invulnerability; instead, we prioritize practical, layered security engineering.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Core Principle 1: Client-Side Isolation -->
      <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400">🛡️</span> 1. Client-Side Static QR Isolation
        </h2>
        <p>
          The most effective way to protect sensitive data is to avoid receiving it in the first place:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 pl-2">
          <li><strong>Local Browser Rendering:</strong> Static QR code calculation and rendering occur entirely in the user’s local browser runtime via open-source JavaScript libraries (<code class="text-xs bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">qr-code-styling</code> and <code class="text-xs bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">qrcode-generator</code>).</li>
          <li><strong>Zero Payload Transit:</strong> Wi-Fi network credentials, personal contact entries (vCards), raw text, and phone numbers entered into the static generator are never sent across the network to our backend servers.</li>
          <li><strong>Client-Side Image Processing:</strong> Logos embedded in static QR codes are read into memory using the browser's native <code class="text-xs">FileReader</code> API without triggering any server uploads.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Core Principle 2: Network & Transport Security -->
      <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400">🔒</span> 2. Transport &amp; Network Security
        </h2>
        <p>
          The website and edge API endpoints are fronted by Cloudflare’s global infrastructure:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 pl-2">
          <li><strong>Mandatory TLS:</strong> All HTTP traffic is automatically redirected to HTTPS using modern Transport Layer Security (TLS 1.3 / TLS 1.2).</li>
          <li><strong>DDoS Mitigation:</strong> Cloudflare edge proxy provides automated network-layer and application-layer DDoS mitigation.</li>
          <li><strong>Strict Headers:</strong> Responses include security headers to mitigate common web application attacks, including anti-MIME-sniffing and cross-origin resource isolation where applicable.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Core Principle 3: Authentication & Session Security -->
      <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400">🔑</span> 3. Authentication &amp; Credential Protection
        </h2>
        <p>
          For users who register an account to manage dynamic QR codes:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 pl-2">
          <li><strong>Cryptographic Password Hashing:</strong> Passwords are never stored in plain text. They are hashed using PBKDF2 with 100,000 iterations and a unique salt via the Web Crypto API (<code class="text-xs bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">crypto.subtle.deriveBits</code>).</li>
          <li><strong>HTTP-Only Session Cookies:</strong> Authentication tokens are signed JSON Web Tokens (JWT) stored in cookies marked with <code class="text-xs bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Path=/</code> (and <code class="text-xs bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">Secure</code> on production HTTPS). This prevents browser scripts from reading or stealing session tokens via XSS.</li>
          <li><strong>Stateless Verification:</strong> Session tokens are verified cryptographically on each authenticated request using HMAC SHA-256 signing keys.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Core Principle 4: Application & Data Protection -->
      <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400">⚙️</span> 4. Application Defenses &amp; Data Sanitization
        </h2>
        <p>
          Our application implements multiple layers of input and database defenses:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 pl-2">
          <li><strong>Parameterized SQL Queries:</strong> All interactions with Cloudflare D1 use prepared statements with bound parameters (<code class="text-xs bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">db.prepare(...).bind(...)</code>), mitigating SQL injection vulnerabilities.</li>
          <li><strong>Strict URI Scheme Filtering:</strong> Dangerous URL schemes (such as <code class="text-xs">javascript:</code>, <code class="text-xs">data:</code>, <code class="text-xs">vbscript:</code>, and <code class="text-xs">file:</code>) are strictly rejected during URL validation to prevent script execution on scanning devices.</li>
          <li><strong>SVG Content Neutralization:</strong> Uploaded SVG logo files are sanitized to remove <code class="text-xs">&lt;script&gt;</code> tags, inline DOM event handlers (e.g., <code class="text-xs">onload</code>, <code class="text-xs">onclick</code>), and <code class="text-xs">&lt;foreignObject&gt;</code> containers.</li>
          <li><strong>Access Control &amp; IDOR Mitigation:</strong> Database mutations on QR codes, assets, and user profiles explicitly verify user ownership (<code class="text-xs">user_id = ?</code>) or require administrative privileges before executing modifications or deletions.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Core Principle 5: Edge Telemetry & IP Anonymization -->
      <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400">📊</span> 5. Dynamic QR Scan Telemetry &amp; IP Anonymization
        </h2>
        <p>
          To protect end users who scan dynamic QR codes:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 pl-2">
          <li><strong>Zero Raw IP Storage:</strong> Incoming client IP addresses are not stored in the database. Instead, the IP address is combined with a daily rotating salt and hashed into a truncated 16-hex-character identifier via SHA-256 for unique visitor metrics.</li>
          <li><strong>Coarse Geolocation Only:</strong> Location data is limited to country, region, and city as reported by Cloudflare edge headers. No high-precision GPS coordinates are collected or stored.</li>
          <li><strong>Decoupled Analytics Failure:</strong> Logging failures do not impact redirect speed or functionality; dynamic QR redirection always takes priority.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Core Principle 6: Third-Party & Payment Security -->
      <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400">💳</span> 6. Payment &amp; Financial Security Boundaries
        </h2>
        <p>
          FreeQRCode-Generator.com intentionally isolates financial operations:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 pl-2">
          <li><strong>Merchant of Record:</strong> Premium subscriptions are billed and processed by Lemon Squeezy. No credit card details, debit card numbers, or CVVs ever touch our servers or databases.</li>
          <li><strong>Payment QR Codes:</strong> UPI, PayPal, Venmo, Cash App, and Zelle generators merely format standard URI schemes and URLs. We do NOT process payments, escrow funds, or interface with bank accounts.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Core Principle 7: Vulnerability Disclosure -->
      <section class="space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400">🚨</span> 7. Vulnerability Reporting &amp; Responsible Disclosure
        </h2>
        <p>
          We welcome vulnerability disclosures from security researchers and users. If you discover a potential security issue, please report it through our contact channel with sufficient technical details to reproduce the issue.
        </p>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800/60 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 space-y-2">
          <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">How to Report:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-xs">
            <li>Submit details via our <a href="/contact" class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 underline font-semibold">Contact Page</a> or <a href="/report-problem" class="text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 underline font-semibold">Report a Problem form</a>.</li>
            <li>Direct email: <a href="mailto:support@freeqrcode-generator.com" class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 underline font-semibold">support@freeqrcode-generator.com</a>.</li>
            <li>Include step-by-step reproduction instructions, HTTP request/response samples, and impact assessment.</li>
            <li>Please allow reasonable time for remediation before any public disclosure.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Backlinks -->
      <div class="border-t border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800 pt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-xs">
        <a href="/privacy" class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 hover:underline font-semibold">&larr; Privacy Policy</a>
        <a href="/methodology" class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 hover:underline font-semibold">QR Methodology &rarr;</a>
        <a href="/data-sources" class="text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 hover:underline font-semibold">Data &amp; Standards &rarr;</a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
